NAME
    hier - EmuSen and DianaSh filesystem layout

SYNOPSIS
    man hier

DESCRIPTION
    EmuSen's directory tree is managed by Galaxia. Inside DianaSh, '/'
    is EmuSen's home directory (<root>/home), not the host operating
    system root. Every file-taking shell command resolves paths through
    this sandbox and refuses any path above '/', regardless of '..'
    segments. The sandbox checks path text rather than resolving
    symbolic links.

    USER DATA DIRECTORIES (UNDER '/')
    /                   Shell root and EmuSen home (<root>/home). Running
                        cd(1) with no arguments returns here.
    /Games              ROM and disc library.
    /Saves              Battery-backed save files (.srm, memory cards),
                        organized per console.
    /Saves/Save States  Save-state snapshots.
    /Library            Application databases (games.db, records.db).
    /Screenshots        Captured screenshots.
    /Artwork            Scraped or user-supplied artwork.
    /Media              Game media assets (covers, videos, manuals).
    /Firmware           User-supplied console firmware and BIOS files.
    /Shaders            Downloaded or custom shader packs.
    /Themes             Installed Qt/QML theme packages (theme.json plus
                        screens/ and assets/) and ES-DE themes.
    /Cheats             User cheat files (.cht). See cheat(1).
    /Cores              User-installed and managed core libraries.
                        Approvals are recorded by SHA-256 hash in
                        /etc/EmuSen/cores.approved. See cores(1).
    /Logs               Debug dumps, load files, and diagnostic logs.
    /Unpacked           Archives unpacked on demand for play.
    /Packages           Self-contained game packages, one directory per
                        game. See pkg(1).
    /Compressed         CHD disc images converted from the library. See
                        chd(1).
    /etc/EmuSen         JSON configuration files (appsettings.json,
                        audio.json, graphics.json, input bindings,
                        cores.approved, cheats/, dianash/trusted).
                        Plain JSON tolerating comments and trailing
                        commas.

    HOST AND MIGRATION DIRECTORIES (OUTSIDE '/')
    The following Galaxia directories sit outside the shell sandbox and
    are used by EmuSen at startup, packaging, or migration time:

    Root                Tree root containing home/. Located once at
                        startup from the executable's directory by
                        walking up to 10 parents for a root marker
                        ('.dianashroot', '.dianaosroot', or source tree
                        marker), falling back to 'DianaShRoot/' beside
                        the binary (or existing 'DianaOSRoot/'). On
                        macOS, an app bundle (.app/Contents/MacOS) and
                        unmarked installs use
                        '~/Library/Application Support/EmuSen'.
    Seed                Read-only seed tree (Contents/Resources/home)
                        bundled inside a macOS .app package, if present.
    ConfigPrevious      Previous config location (<root>/etc/EmuSen)
                        used before configuration moved under home/.
    ConfigLegacy        Host per-user config directory
                        (<application_data>/EmuSen: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME or
                        ~/.config on Linux, Application Support on
                        macOS, roaming AppData on Windows) checked for
                        first-run migration.
    LegacyRoot          Earlier home path checked during one-time data
                        migration.
    LogDefault          Fallback application log root
                        (<application_data>/EmuSen/Logs).

    Shipped shell modules, programs, and manual pages live in the
    'dianash/' folder beside the running executable (with manual pages
    under 'dianash/man/'), outside the shell sandbox.

EXAMPLES
    man hier
    ls /
    cd /Logs && ls

SEE ALSO
    cd(1), ls(1), pwd(1), dianash(1), modules(7)
